Upstream: M-HT/SR ac690ddf3010bc3d2c875cb1b5e8da4f53a8d5b3, after sr-llasm.patch.
Original: LLasm opens local paths through Phobos POSIX filesystem APIs.
Replacement: a bounded stdin virtual-file adapter and explicit exit status.
Effect: the unchanged LLasm parser and IR generator run in browser-d WebAssembly.
Why: the browser has no host filesystem or POSIX environment symbols.
Evidence: native GDC and browser DMD emit byte-identical synthetic and full-game
IR with -m64 -inline-idiv -pic -ptrofs -O. The adapter accepts only flat inputs,
limits file counts/sizes, rejects duplicates/truncation and forwards failures.
This patch retains upstream's MIT notice. The adapter is distributed under MIT.

